From 12fb47ed09d50d18ae052a624d14301bdf54d735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): [daveey] delegate children get their own
 terminal snapshot; --board works from worker shells; boards list counts each
 board

- delegate_task children share the parent's terminal environment, whose bash
  snapshot is sourced before every command, so a child's export (e.g.
  HERMES_KANBAN_DB=.../runners/kanban.db) reached the parent's shell. Each
  child now reads/writes its own overlay snapshot (read-through to the
  enclosing child, then the parent); the parent snapshot also drops
  HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_OWNER.
- A worker shell's explicit 'hermes kanban --board B' now resolves to B's own
  DB when it lies inside the delegate fence root (reads follow the flag,
  writes stay refused); dispatched-worker tools, in-process children and
  machine flows stay pinned.
- 'boards list' counts each board's own DB instead of the env pin.
- 'kanban list' skips its best-effort recompute_ready write in a fenced shell
  instead of failing.
- The CLI refusal names the worker/delegate fence and points to the kanban_*
  tools; the env -u bypass is documented as an accepted limit of a
  cooperative same-uid fence.
---
